From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:15:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-pci: stop Apple ANS before a restart as before a kexec

A restart that re-enters the boot loader (PSCI SYSTEM_RESET to m1n1)
leaves the S8003 ANS controller to a loader that brings its port up again
and reads from it. On a plain shutdown nvme_disable_prepare_reset() sets
SHN but keeps CC.EN, and power-cycling the port in that state hangs the
SoC.

Take the paired, certified stop that a kexec handoff already uses on every
restart as well: drain, SHN, CC.EN and RDY clear, bus mastering off and the
NVMMU/DART retired. Such a failure is not a sleep refusal, so it no longer
takes the sleep branch; it ends in a cold watchdog reset, as for kexec.
Power-off and halt keep the existing shutdown.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
index 6868811d5..9fe60de0e 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
@@ -3381,7 +3381,7 @@ static int nvme_dev_disable_paired(struct nvme_dev *dev, bool shutdown, bool pai
 	enum nvme_ctrl_state state = nvme_ctrl_state(&dev->ctrl);
 	struct pci_dev *pdev = to_pci_dev(dev->dev);
 	bool dead;
-	bool for_sleep = paired && !kexec_in_progress;
+	bool for_sleep = paired && !kexec_in_progress && system_state != SYSTEM_RESTART;
 	int ret = paired ? -EBUSY : 0;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev->shutdown_lock);
@@ -4053,14 +4053,23 @@ static void nvme_reset_done(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 		flush_work(&dev->ctrl.reset_work);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A restart re-enters the boot loader, which starts the storage port again
+ * and reads from the controller. It needs the controller stopped as iBoot
+ * leaves it (SHN complete, CC.EN and RDY clear, DMA certified stopped): the
+ * stop a kexec handoff takes. Anything less ends in a cold reset.
+ */
 static void nvme_shutdown(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 {
 	struct nvme_dev *dev = pci_get_drvdata(pdev);
+	bool restart = !kexec_in_progress && system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART;
 
-	if (kexec_in_progress && apple_ans_is_s8003(dev->dev) &&
+	if ((kexec_in_progress || restart) && apple_ans_is_s8003(dev->dev) &&
 	    dev->dma_ops == &nvme_pci_apple_ans_ops && !apple_ans_handoff_begin(dev->dev)) {
 		if (!nvme_wait_reset(&dev->ctrl) || nvme_dev_disable_paired(dev, true, true)) {
-			apple_cold_reset("Apple ANS: refusing unsafe powered kexec handoff");
+			apple_cold_reset(restart ?
+					 "Apple ANS: unsafe controller stop before restart" :
+					 "Apple ANS: refusing unsafe powered kexec handoff");
 			return;
 		}
 		return;
